On-Prem vs. SaaS, PaaS, IaaS – Know the Difference 💡
When it comes to IT infrastructure, understanding where responsibility lies is key

🔒 On-Prem:
Everything is managed by you: hardware, software, networking, security.
Full control, but also full responsibility.

🖥️ SaaS (Software as a Service):
You just use the app. Everything else is managed for you.
Example: Microsoft 365, Salesforce

🧱 PaaS (Platform as a Service):
You focus on the app, code, and data.
Provider manages servers, OS, and runtime.
Example: Azure App Services

☁️ IaaS (Infrastructure as a Service):
You manage the OS, apps, and data.
Cloud provider handles the hardware.
Example: Azure VMs, AWS EC2
